        {lifestyleComparison.teal.map((item) => (
          <li>{item}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      A useful gut-check: talk to a working merchant navy officer directly about their real experience of a full
      sea contract — not the highlight-reel version, the actual day-to-day reality of months away — before treating
      this as a settled decision. Recruitment marketing rarely surfaces this honestly enough on its own.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="ai-risk">What autonomous shipping and AI actually change, honestly</h2>

  <p>
    Most "is merchant navy a good career" searches skip this question, but autonomous-shipping headlines make it
    worth a direct, honest answer rather than silence.
  </p>

  <p>
    AI leverage on ships today is real but narrow — automated route optimisation, predictive maintenance
    monitoring for engine systems, and AI-assisted weather routing genuinely help officers manage a vessel more
    efficiently. These tools support the officer's decisions; they do not currently make them.
  </p>

  <p>
    The disruption risk from fully autonomous commercial shipping is a genuine long-term industry conversation,
    but it is not a near-term threat to a career started today — autonomous vessel technology remains largely in
    trial and limited-route stages, and international maritime regulation, insurance liability frameworks, and
    port-state safety requirements are not yet structured around removing qualified officers from vessels. A more
    immediate, honest read: officers who build genuine comfort with automated monitoring and routing systems, as
    a normal part of the job rather than something to resist, are better positioned as these tools mature further
    over the coming decade.
  </p>

  <h2 id="growth-scaling">How officers actually scale their careers</h2>

  <p>
    A merchant navy career can plateau exactly like any other job — staying at junior ranks with no deliberate exam
    progression has a real, moderate ceiling. But there is genuine headroom for officers who progress deliberately.
  </p>

